// corpus: known-failure the result type of an overloaded call on an untyped operand is read off one arm (ROADMAP: "Overloaded result type on an unknown operand")
// `slice` is overloaded: a string slice is a string, a list slice is a list.
// With an untyped parameter the static pass types the result as a list, so
// a string consumer refuses it before anything runs. Typing the parameter
// (`s: string`) avoids the error; the untyped program is correct.
firstTwo(s) = characters(slice(s, 1, 2))
firstTwo("abc")
// ➔ ["a", "b"]
